From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:46:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ppp: pppd: hash the host name without signed overflow

pppd seeds its random numbers with a hash of the host name, computed in
an int that overflows for any name longer than six characters: signed
overflow, undefined behaviour. In a UBSan build pppd traps in
magic_init() at every start, and the WAN never comes up.

Add a patch to ppp that hashes in unsigned arithmetic. It is meant for
ppp upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/network/services/ppp/Makefile         |  2 +-
 ...he-host-name-without-signed-overflow.patch | 33 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/network/services/ppp/patches/210-pppd-hash-the-host-name-without-signed-overflow.patch

diff --git a/package/network/services/ppp/Makefile b/package/network/services/ppp/Makefile
index c0da96a..1ee741b 100644
--- a/package/network/services/ppp/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/services/ppp/Makefile
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ include $(INCLUDE_DIR)/kernel.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=ppp
 PKG_VERSION:=2.5.3
-PKG_RELEASE:=3
+PKG_RELEASE:=4
 
 PKG_SOURCE:=$(PKG_NAME)-$(PKG_VERSION).tar.gz
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://download.samba.org/pub/ppp
diff --git a/package/network/services/ppp/patches/210-pppd-hash-the-host-name-without-signed-overflow.patch b/package/network/services/ppp/patches/210-pppd-hash-the-host-name-without-signed-overflow.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..42e747b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/network/services/ppp/patches/210-pppd-hash-the-host-name-without-signed-overflow.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] pppd: hash the host name without signed overflow
+
+get_host_seed() hashes the host name into an int, h = h * 37 + c, which
+overflows for any name longer than six characters: signed overflow,
+undefined behaviour. Built with -fsanitize=undefined
+-fsanitize-trap=undefined, pppd traps in magic_init() at every start on
+a router named "OpenWrt" or longer.
+
+Hash in unsigned arithmetic, which wraps, and take each character as
+unsigned, as a hash of bytes should.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/pppd/sys-linux.c
++++ b/pppd/sys-linux.c
+@@ -3686,13 +3686,13 @@
+ int
+ get_host_seed(void)
+ {
+-    int h;
++    unsigned int h;
+     const char *p;
+ 
+     h = 407;
+     for (p = hostname; *p != 0; ++p)
+-	h = h * 37 + *p;
+-    return h;
++	h = h * 37 + (unsigned char) *p;
++    return (int) h;
+ }
+ 
+ /********************************************************************
